<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάκλᾰ-σις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακλάω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a bending back, flexure,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				2
			</span></i>; of swords, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.30
			</span></i>; <i>curve,</i> of the lines of a ship, <i><span class="en">
				Callix.
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>reflection</i> of light or <i>reverberation</i> of sound, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>AP</u>
				0.98a29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sens.</u>
				437b10
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.199
			</span></i>; so of the wind, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				945a7
			</span></i>; of water, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ποιεῖσθαι</span>
			have its course <i>turned,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.43.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῆς σαρκὸς ποιεῖσθαι</span>
			make it <i>elastic,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				966b17
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
